  "note": "mechanical checks by tools/merge_delivery.py; mathematics reviewed in full by NT-cc-Q31-c37c0c4be (reviewer sub-agent of L); spot-checked: I read the whole delivery: the item, both new nodes, every cited node's statement, the Mathlib sources (Presheaf.lean:77-96, Type.lean:158-167, LocallyPresentable.lean:30-90) and the blueprint ancestor's proof paragraph 2. HTT is not archived locally (the worker filed a WANTED request) and I could not open the PDF, so I checked the cited places (A.2.4.2, A.2.8.2/4/5, A.3.3.2/4) from my knowledge of the book. The item statement is unchanged and correct. Edge cases checked: empty D, terminal D, discrete two-object D, the arrow category, D=BG, and the n=0 boundary inclusion. Steps 1-5 and 7 are sound: local presentability, Kan left properness/combinatoriality/simplicial axiom, the free-diagram adjunction L_d -| ev_d, the small-object argument with a regular bound, and the model axioms via the retract argument. One repair (error E5/C2): step 6 extended the simplicial pushout-product axiom from generators to all projective cofibrations by asserting, without argument, that pushout product carries cell presentations to cell presentations. I rewrote step 6 to argue directly: by the tensor/cotensor adjunction, lifting i□j against p is equivalent to lifting i against p^{□j}, which at each object is the Kan map of Step 2. This gives cases (a) p trivial, (b) j trivial, (c) i trivial, then the mapping-space form. The step now uses lem-coef-kan-quillen-right-proper only; proof_deps is unchanged. New node lem-coef-all-cofibrant-left-proper is true, general, not a clause of the item and not in Mathlib or the DAG. New node lem-coef-presheaf-local-presentability is a valid two-clause Mathlib leaf; applying it to SSet.{u} with u>0 will need a universe lift in Lean (stage-2 note only). All cited nodes are in the unit, so no tool uses. Separately, the existing unsplit node lem-coef-simplicial-model-coherent-diagrams generalizes the item; that is for maintainer awareness only and does not affect this split. The corrected item is in fixes/dag/nodes/sec-six-functors/ and the full review is in review.md.; 1 file(s) fixed by the reviewer"
